##Day 10 Notes – Creating Elements with JavaScript

createElement
const li = document.createElement("li");
Creates a new HTML element.
textContent
li.textContent = "Python";
Adds text inside the element.
appendChild
skillList.appendChild(li);
Adds the new element to the page.
innerHTML = ""
skillList.innerHTML = "";
Clears all old content inside an element.
Full Pattern
const list = document.querySelector("#skills ul");
list.innerHTML = "";

for (let skill of skills) {
const li = document.createElement("li");
li.textContent = skill;
list.appendChild(li);
}
Key Point:
JavaScript can create new HTML elements and add them to the page dynamically.


Example;
script.js:
'''
// Skills Array
const skills = ["Python", "SQL", "HTML", "CSS", "JavaScript", "Git", "Networking"];

// Show Skills on Page
const skillList = document.querySelector("#skills ul");
skillList.innerHTML = ""; // Clear old items

for (let skill of skills) {
  const li = document.createElement("li");
  li.textContent = skill;
  skillList.appendChild(li);
}

// Projects Array
const projects = [
  {
    title: "Portfolio Website",
    tech: "HTML, CSS, JavaScript"
  },
  {
    title: "Todo App",
    tech: "JavaScript"
  }
];

// Show Projects on Page
const projectList = document.querySelector("#projects ul");
projectList.innerHTML = ""; // Clear old items

for (let project of projects) {
  const li = document.createElement("li");
  li.textContent = `${project.title} (${project.tech})`;
  projectList.appendChild(li);
}
'''

