# Day 10 — Burp Repeater Quick Notes

## Repeater

Used to **manually edit and resend individual HTTP requests**.

```text
Proxy → Capture → Send to Repeater
                 ↓
              Modify
                 ↓
               Send
                 ↓
             Compare
```

## Parameter

A value sent to the server to tell it what to process.

Example:

```http
GET /product?id=42
```

```text
id = parameter
42 = value
```

Parameters can appear in:

* URL/query
* POST body
* JSON
* Cookies
* Headers

## Response Testing

After changing an input, compare:

* Status code
* Response length
* Response body
* Headers
* Error messages

## Testing Rule

**Change one thing at a time** → easier to identify what caused the response change.

## Proxy vs Repeater

```text
Proxy    → intercepts live browser traffic
Repeater → manually edits/resends copied requests
```

## Core Pentesting Workflow

```text
Capture → Understand → Modify ONE input → Send → Compare → Assess
```

**Safety:** Only test your own applications or authorized labs.
